Upstream models

PPWR Compliance Screener sends prompts to an OpenAI-compatible endpoint that you configure and hold the key
for - a local runtime, a hosted provider, a router, or a proxy of your own. The lab does not train,
fine-tune or distribute models, and is not a provider of a general-purpose AI model under the EU AI
Act; obligations for the model itself rest with whoever provides it, under their own terms.

A model is used for exactly two bounded jobs: reading an uploaded document into structured fields,
and writing the covering paragraph of a gap notice. No model produces a pass or a fail. Verdicts
come from a deterministic rule engine evaluating a versioned JSON ruleset, and swapping the model
cannot change one.

Output drafted through that endpoint is marked per Article 50. See COMPLIANCE.md.

